      <floats-group id="article-38850.s20">
        <fig id="article-38850.image.f4" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Role of RANKL/RANK/OPG Axis on Bone Homeostasis and Immune System. RANKL is secreted by osteoblasts and osteocytes when stimulated by parathyroid hormone (PTH), vitamin D, and/or prostaglandin 2 (PGE2). RANKL binds to RANK on the membrane of osteoclast progenitors (preosteoclasts), which results in bone resorption by mature osteoclasts. Osteoprotegerin (OPG) binds to RANKL, thus inhibiting RANK signaling and bone resorption. RANK/RANKL also plays a role in immune cell regulation and the crosstalk between both systems (termed osteoimmunology). <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/oncology/articles/10.3389/fonc.2020.01283/full">Frontiers in Oncology</ext-link></p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="RoleofRANKL" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-38850.s21">
        <fig id="article-38850.image.f5" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Lifestyle and Nutritional Optimization for Bone Health for All Postmenopausal Women. This chart guides women with osteoporosis with nutrition and lifestyle choice information. Shoback D, Rosen CJ, Black DM, Cheung AM, Murad MH, Eastell R.&#x000a0;Pharmacological management of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women: an endocrine society guideline update.&#x000a0;<italic toggle="yes">J Clin Endocrinol Metab.</italic> 2020;105(3):587&#x02013;594.&#x000a0;doi: <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://academic.oup.com/jcem/article/105/3/587/5739968">10.1210/clinem/dgaa048</ext-link>.</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Updated" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
